SUMMARY:Deadline: Toronto Arts Council: Media Artists Program - Creation 20
 26
DESCRIPTION:Project funding from the Toronto Arts Council for professional 
 media artists to create or complete independent film\, video\, audio\, dig
 ital\, VR/AR and multimedia works\, with grants up to $15\,000. ELIGIBILIT
 Y: Canadian citizens\, permanent residents or Protected Persons who have l
 ived in Toronto for at least one year\, are professional media artists ret
 aining full creative control\, and are not students.\n\nOrganisation: Toro
 nto Arts Council\nLocation: Toronto\, Canada\nAward: Up to $15\,000 (CAD) 
 per artist for media-arts creation. No application fee.\nDuration: Per pro
 ject\n\nMore: https://torontoartscouncil.org/grants/media-artists-program-
 creation/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://torontoartscouncil.org/grants/media-artists-program-creation/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Toronto\, Canada
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vimeo-short-film-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T121219Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
SUMMARY:Deadline: Vimeo Short Film Grant (USD 60\,000 for 5 filmmakers)
DESCRIPTION:Vimeo's Short Film Grant awards five emerging filmmakers USD 60
 \,000 in cash each to produce a short film\, alongside mentorship from cel
 ebrated filmmakers\, a loaned Panavision camera package\, OWC storage hard
 ware\, a one-year Vimeo Advanced subscription\, and distribution on Vimeo 
 with in-person screenings. ELIGIBILITY: residents of the United States or 
 Canada\, at least 18 years old\, who are emerging filmmakers having direct
 ed at least two short films but no feature films\; a valid Vimeo account i
 s required. TIMELINE: winners announced by 15 March 2027\; production must
  be completed by September 2027 and post-production by March 2028. HOW TO 
 APPLY: via SlideRoom with project details\, an artist statement\, team bio
 s\, creative materials (screenplay or treatment)\, a budget proposal\, a p
 roduction timeline and mentorship goals. No fee to apply. DEADLINE: 16 Oct
 ober 2026 at 11:59 PM ET (opened 21 September 2026).\n\nOrganisation: Vime
 o\nLocation: Online application. Open to residents of the United States an
 d Canada.\nAward: Five filmmakers each receive USD 60\,000 in cash for pro
 duction\, plus a one-year Vimeo Advanced subscription\, mentorship from ce
 lebrated filmmakers\, a loaned Panavision camera package\, OWC storage har
 dware\, and distribution on Vimeo with in-person screenings. Free to apply
 .\nDuration: Production must be completed by September 2027 and post-produ
 ction by March 2028\; winners announced by 15 March 2027\n\nMore: https://
 vimeo.com/shortfilmgrant?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://vimeo.com/shortfilmgrant?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online application. Open to residents of the United States and Can
 ada.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oac-media-artists-creation-2026-oct@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T121219Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261008
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261009
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ontario Arts Council: Media Artists Creation Projects (Oc
 tober 2026 deadline)
DESCRIPTION:Production and post-production grants for independent media art
 works: film\, video\, animation\, audio art\, digital media\, VR/AR and mu
 ltimedia installation. Two streams by career stage: Emerging media artists
  can request up to CAD 10\,000\; Mid-Career and Established artists up to 
 CAD 40\,000. ELIGIBILITY: Ontario-resident directors or principal media ar
 tists who hold copyright of the work\; currently enrolled students are not
  eligible in the Emerging stream. Deadlines recur (March and October)\; th
 is round closes 8 October 2026 at 1 p.m. ET.\n\nOrganisation: Ontario Arts
  Council\nLocation: Ontario\, Canada. Ontario-resident directors/principal
  media artists only.\nAward: Emerging: maximum CAD 10\,000\; Mid-Career an
 d Established: maximum CAD 40\,000. No application fee.\nDuration: Per pro
 ject\n\nMore: https://www.arts.on.ca/grants/media-artists-creation-project
 s?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.arts.on.ca/grants/media-artists-creation-projects?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ontario\, Canada. Ontario-resident directors/principal media artis
 ts only.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:manitoba-create-grant-2026-oct@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261010T121219Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
SUMMARY:Deadline: Manitoba Arts Council: Create Grant (October 2026 intake)
DESCRIPTION:Research and creation of new work\, or development of works in 
 progress\, by professional artists in all disciplines including media arts
 \; creation-based residencies are also fundable. Professional fees and hon
 orariums are a required budget line\, so the money genuinely pays the arti
 st. Amounts rise with career stage: up to CAD 7\,500 (emerging)\, CAD 10\,
 000 (mid-career) or CAD 15\,000 (established). ELIGIBILITY: individuals mu
 st have been resident in Manitoba for at least one year. Deadlines recur (
 March 20 and October 10)\; this round closes 10 October 2026.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: Manitoba Arts Council\nLocation: Manitoba\, Canada. Applicants must h
 ave been Manitoba residents for at least one year.\nAward: Emerging: up to
  CAD 7\,500\; Mid-career: up to CAD 10\,000\; Established: up to CAD 15\,0
 00. No application fee.\nDuration: Per project\n\nMore: https://artscounci
 l.mb.ca/grants/create/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://artscouncil.mb.ca/grants/create/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Manitoba\, Canada. Applicants must have been Manitoba residents fo
 r at least one year.
END:VEVENT
